<br>
Step 1 - <br>
<br>
If you are interested in joining Abyss you need to start a thread here about who you are, how you play, etc etc. Things that must be included are....<br>
1. Level/class (minimum level is now 54 for Abyss)<br>
2. What other guilds you have been in<br>
3. How much and when you like to play<br>
4. What draws you to Abyss<br>
<br>
As soon as you have told us something about yourself, go to the raid section and sign up. Make sure you post in your sign-up that you are interested in membership (that way when making the lists the Leader knows to select you for a team).<br>
<br>
Step 2 -<br>
<br>
An officer will post your name in the New Member Section. You must get 3 sponsors among members. A member can only have one sponsor per trial period so this may be hard to do. You must work hard to get the support of a sponsor. Once you have 3 sponsors an officer will invite you for the trial period. During the trial period you get to know us and we get to know you. Come on as many raids as you can (we like to raid a lot). During this trial period your sponsors will be responsible for making sure you know when raids are, to get you acclimated, to work out any concers or questions you have....they are here to make your trial period easier on you =). But, you need to know the whole guild because of step 3...<br>
<br>
Step 3 -<br>
<br>
After two weeks you will be voted upon in a forum you cannot access until you are a full member. More then 5 'Need to know him/her better' votes and you have 2 more weeks of trial period. Then another vote takes place. More then 3 no votes and you will not become a full member. You may at any time redo the trial period in order to fix whatever was seemingly broken. Members are given 2 days to vote so you will know quickly what the decision of the guild was.<br>
<br>
This our new policy, we may tweak it some depending on how it works out =). Hope to see you in game!<br>
<br>
<br>
 <p>Aislinn Darkenwald<br>
Level 56 Druid<br>
